 your pointer finger and  press down now we can grab it  right here and we can slide our thumb  out now just flatten this portion out  again  now we're going to take the portion that  we just folded down and we're going to  tuck it  into the center of the ring inside  so just take it and round it off a  little bit like this  and tuck it to the inside just like that  and tuck it all the way up to this edge  here  so just push it all the way through and  give it a good pinch right here  and you'll see we have this excess here  now we could press this excess  again on top so we kind of wrapped it  around  and we're just going to press it on top  like that and give it a good pinch  now you'll see we should be able to  actually fit the ring to our finger  this actually can slide now through this  little box that we made  so as you'll see it can slide back and  forth  and what we're going to do is we're just  going to open it a little bit  and just try our finger on so just see  it fits pretty well i'm just going to  take it off  the amount of excess here should be a  little bit wider  than the box here maybe a quarter of an  inch once it's just like that  we're going to take this excess and  we're going to fold it on top  of this little piece right here so just  fold it right on top of the box to the  left  and as you'll see there's a little bit  of excess sticking over the left edge  here  we're just going to hold it like this  upside down  and this is the excess portion that we  need to get right in here  so to do that take your pointer finger  and push in here and make a  dent so you're just going to kind of  dent it like that  open it up a little bit and now we could  take this corner  and we're going to squish it in there  just press it in there like that  really hard do the same with the other  corner  so it's all the way in there and now we  could take that dent  and just flatten it or pop it back out  and what that does is it actually locks  the ring in place  so now you'll see we have a ring that  should fit your finger now we can make  the ninja star  now that we have the ring we can make  the mini ninja star and as you can see  it is very small  but i have faith in my subscribers  because i've taught this ninja star a  bunch of times it's special because it  has a little sleeve  on the back of it here as you could see  the back is different than the front  and it's that sleeve that allows it to  join to the origami ring just like that  and that way it can kind of be  interlocked as you can see  so let's make the ninja star now to make  it we just need to take the square that  we had before  fold it in half and then we can crease  it  and tear it in half when we do that  we'll get two equal sheets and i'm going  to be using colored paper here just  because it's easier to demonstrate and  what we're going to do  is take it and hold them so that the  little triangle here the crease is on  the bottom right of both pieces  and they're both going to be made the  same way so i'm just going to go through  one of them  and then i'll quickly do the other one  we're going to take the top edge and  fold it down to the bottom edge just  like this  and align them as neatly as you can make  a crease  and then we can take the left edge and  fold it across to the right edge  once again make a crease now you can  unfold it  and we can flip it upside down and  you'll see the reason i positioned it  like that is because we have a small  crease in the paper so we're just going  to take the right side and fold it down  on that crease  so that the top edge is on that vertical  line so the right side goes down  the left side goes up so left  up right down then we could flip it  upside down  and you'll see we have these two little  boxes we're going to take the upper  right corner  fold it down to the lower left corner  just like that and then take the lower  left corner  and fold it up to the upper right  corner like that then we could take the  two  triangles that we have here and as  you'll see it makes a  z and we'll fold these two triangles  inwards to the middle so now that we  finish that piece  let's make the other one really quickly  so just make another identical piece  by folding in half both ways the left  side goes up the right side goes down  flip it fold the boxes inwards and then  the triangles in  and now we're ready to interlock them to  complete the ninja star ring  to interlock the pieces with the ring  grab the ring and hold it so that the  box is facing downwards and grab one of  the pieces  open up the flaps so that they're facing  towards you and slide it  underneath the band so that you have two  flaps on either side  and you can kind of close them like this  you might have to adjust them a little  bit later  but just make sure that you can fold  them completely downwards  then you could open them back up and  grab the other piece  and we're also going to open up the  flaps gently and  hold it so that this piece in the middle  this middle  part is parallel with the band and it  sort of forms an  x with the other piece once you have it  like this  we can close all four of the flaps now  in a clockwise direction  starting with this one so that's one  then we'll go to this one  two three you might have to adjust it  you might have to kind of bend it a  little farther  finally the last one is going to go over  this one  and kind of into here just lift up this  one a little bit so just lift up the  first one  so that you can kind of see the pocket  there see it  and then curve this one over  the third one and underneath and then  slide that one back in and then you can  just work it all together like this  adjust it as necessary and you have  completed the ninja star ring  so let's see how it looks and it looks  pretty awesome  if you were interested in making the  bracelet you can take the sheet holding  it like this and splitting it in  quarters to get a longer section  then just use 